This skill documents the HyperFrames command-line tool (npm package
"hyperframes", https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes), which is licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0. No HyperFrames code is included here.

The composition rules, attribute names, command names, flags and the
project skeleton in references/composition.md were derived from the
HyperFrames 0.9.98 package and its bundled documentation (Apache-2.0),
then checked by running the 0.9.98 CLI. The text was rewritten, not copied.

Changes made relative to that documentation:
- Rewritten in our own words and reduced to the rules we use.
- Telemetry, usage beacons, feedback submissions, uploads, cloud rendering
  and self-update are turned off or excluded.
- The CLI is run from a pinned local install (npx --no), never fetched
  at runtime.
- Scripts and fonts are vendored into the project so renders stay offline.

